  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nEight additional dirty aliases on the pinned PR2462 words, followed by a new whole-call owner schedule, give **conditional \u03ba \u2248 0.0017137379215475043**, about **0.59058% above the pinned PR2474 comparison claim**. The exact rational is in `research/source-partner-lifetimes/CLAIM.json`.\n\nRestore jointly recoverable source partners before handoffs destroy required reads, transport exact target residuals through the target precondition, and derive inverse cleanup from the changed word. Helpers fall from 430 to 422 per call. Both orientations are checked on all 646 independent inputs; all 78 cold endpoints and private cleanup buffers remain charged. The diagonal call order and literal fill admit all 281,052 whole-helper roles.\n\nThe full global paid profile is `{1:1599730, 2:420912, 3:219782, 4:78588, 5:17756, 7:5328, 8:114, 16:172, 32:3, 48:26488}`. There are 74 replicas, 666 calls, dimension 73, live stock 66304, physical stock 66814, deficit 23680, and charged prefix reserve 2048 bits. The exact hosted rank mass is 4,816,512. The supplier endpoint is 0.001713737921547504346752; exact outer refinement establishes the final claim.\n\nThis is a conditional finite construction with exact outer arithmetic. Inherited all-size/compiler, common-label/mutable-source, realization, precision/exact-recovery, analytic, and other multiplication-theorem obligations remain. No independent human review or complete multiplication theorem is claimed. The selected frontier is unchanged.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nExplicit user assignment; task `complex-new-helper-inventory`, scope refined to recoverable source-partner lifetimes and physical rehosting. This changes the local inventory before optimizing the fully hosted recursive moment. Main base: `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`; the source-partner package starts from preceding local package commit `930a1d0ab9b1562ce925118b3654d94b24e6e9ab`.\n\nPinned supplier: #2462 at `ef34071fee6dfb0286e9850a5cec4e36d9eb126d`, reconstructed byte-for-byte from #2435 at `324d7d3590dc21003940a44cb0cbdc32b3620f25` plus a hash-bound 40-file overlay. #2474 at `5298f86c5193db65f869121eab3cac16d557196c` is a claim comparison, not a supplier; its current claim was rechecked before submission. Relative to #2462, this adds eight source aliases and changes the physical schedule. #2474 independently reuses source 31 for helper 637; this word uses source 31 for helper 633 and includes seven other aliases. The explicit centre-only cut guard responds to #2478.\n\nThe branch includes `research/source-partner-lifetimes` and preceding scoped `research/t74-owner-consolidation`, which supplies the immutable PR2435 archive. The latter realizes the four-owner exchange also audited independently in #2442 and #2466 and numerically superseded by the source-partner construction. Frozen predecessors remain unchanged. Full source bindings and predecessor attribution are in the package READMEs and manifests.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Registered bounded replay: exact forward/dual words on all independent inputs, literal physical ownership, and eleven rejecting controls covering source restoration, prelude coefficients, missing roles, windows, and duplicated families.\n- Fresh complete cold replay: retained parent; native base/extra providers; discovery and strict global admission; geometry controls; exact outer ledger and independent balance; all nineteen outer evidence replays, 63 strict inequalities, and seventeen outer rejecting controls.\n- Exact claim/profile/rank-mass and comparison-source bindings; proof-input hashes; package metadata and clean diff. Hosted Linux CI has not been run locally.\n\nBounded checks (Python 3.12, standard library):\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/t74-owner-consolidation\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/source-partner-lifetimes\n```\nComplete cold replay (Python 3.11.11, NumPy 1.26.4, SymPy 1.14.0, SciPy 1.15.3; see package requirements):\n```sh\npython3 -B research/source-partner-lifetimes/full_replay.py --work /fresh/absolute/replay\n```\nEvidence: `research/source-partner-lifetimes/VALIDATION.json`, `receipts/`, and `evidence/`. Archived ephemeral paths are explicitly normalized. The bounded hook is not a substitute for complete native/global/outer admission.\n\n## Credit\n\nJeremy Kothe/#2462 and #2435; Tekalign/#2436; Vlado Vojdanovski/#2322; Cinna Davis/#2226; Dugongue/#2309; Sagar Thakrar/#2315 and #2442; Marius-Paul Dumitrean/#2478; Rohan Arun and the #1297/#1319 supplier lineage; and retained native/global/outer authors. The READMEs and source archives preserve detailed attribution and notices.\n\nPrepared with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance at the user's direction. No subagents or independent human review. Apache-2.0, with predecessor notices retained.\n\n## Open next questions\n\nSee `research/source-partner-lifetimes/README.md`: improve the changed-word fill through diagonal-order variants and residual concentration; test lender reassignment with displaced helpers explicitly reintroduced; or derive low-frame inverse rows for larger jointly recoverable source subspaces. The first needs a sharper exact feasible fill; the latter two need a complete changed word and native/global admission. The remaining fixed-word packing gap is small, so substantial further gains require a new local inventory.\n",
